# Build context filter for tools/deployment/Dockerfile (T20). BuildKit, the default builder since
# Docker 23, reads <Dockerfile name>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile in preference to a
# .dockerignore at the context root. The context root is the folder holding the MeshCentral,
# MeshAgent and artifacts checkouts.
#
# Send only what the Dockerfile COPYs. Local server state, backups and secrets (node_modules,
# meshcentral-data with its config.json and keys, server-backups with the database dump,
# branding_config.local.json, sibling checkouts) never enter the build context. The image is
# unchanged: the build reads only the package files, agents/, public/, plugins/ and root .js
# files of MeshCentral, the three listed MeshAgent files, and artifacts/.
*

!MeshCentral
MeshCentral/node_modules
MeshCentral/meshcentral-data
MeshCentral/meshcentral-files
MeshCentral/meshcentral-backups
MeshCentral/meshcentral-recordings
MeshCentral/meshcentral-web
MeshCentral/server-backups

!MeshAgent/deploy.py
!MeshAgent/tools/configure_agent_certificate_history.js
!MeshAgent/tools/prepare_release_image.py

!artifacts
